WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:11.720
Reach for speed, reach for the whistle, go where the rail may run.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:26.030
Reach for the word, reach for the story, follow the rainbow sun station where dreams are.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.180
The railroad told us the repairs would be done in three days.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.280
It's already been six days, and they're still not finished.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.750
Well, the repair crews are doing the best they can,

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.230
and people have to travel in safety.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.610
I know, but the main office sends us a new schedule practically every day.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:56.750
Indian Valley Railroad has to understand that a train schedule is like a promise,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.910
and a promise has to be kept whether it's made by a person.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:08.180
come up with something to help our passengers now just a moment didn't we

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:17.810
say that the 915 to Logan's wash doesn't run on weekends I thought so so

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.560
all right then we're finished for now and about time may I

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:41.870
Oh, that's better. Nothing like a spot of exercise to get the blood running.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:46.050
Do they have these kinds of schedule problems on the island of Sodor?

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:52.250
I should say so. Why, just the other day, it seemed that everybody was late all the time.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.250
Well, here, I'll tell you about it.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.480
The engines were finding life difficult.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.570
Workmen were mending the viaduct on the main line.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.780
The archers needed strengthening,

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:15.170
so Topham Hatt did not want to close the railway while the work was done,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.670
and so repairs took a long time.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:40.480
had to take great care when crossing the viadal and the delay often made them late on their

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.390
journey to the junction where they knew thomas would be ready to collect his passages

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.950
Thomas grew crosser and crosser.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.650
Time's time, he grumbled.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.320
Why should I keep my passengers waiting

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.800
while Henry and James dawdle about all day on viaducts?

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.820
Don't blame me, snorted Henry.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.320
If we hurried across the viaduct, it might collapse,

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.940
and then you'd have no passengers at all.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.420
What would you do then?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.600
Run my train on time for one thing, retorted Thomas.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.280
hurried away before Henry could answer.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.730
Bertie was impatient, too.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:42.180
He was time to arrive just after Thomas.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.950
His passengers found that,

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.650
instead of going straight from the bus to their train,

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.670
they were kept waiting till Thomas arrived.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.400
Soon Bertie grew cross with Thomas.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.510
Late again, he remarked,

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.070
as Thomas panted wearily in.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.120
We may be friends, but I thought you could go fast, Thomas.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:11.480
It's time we had another race.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.450
I reckon I could beat you now.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:19.300
Thomas let off steam, loud rubbish, he hissed fiercely.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.460
It's those mainline engines.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:26.490
They dither about on the viaduct and then blame Sir Topham Hatt's workman.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.980
It's just an excuse for laziness if you...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:44.570
ask me james was later than ever at the junction i'm sorry thomas he puffed i was held up at the

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:52.440
station and the viaduct made it worse it's lucky for you i'm a guaranteed connection grumbled thomas

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:59.920
before james could answer he puffed importantly away come along he

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.200
panted to the coaches.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.940
Annie and Claraville did their best,

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.540
but Thomas soon found that he couldn't save much time.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.000
Suddenly, Thomas saw Bertie ahead.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:17.530
His radiator was steaming.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.010
What's the matter? asked Thomas.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.640
You should be at the station by now.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:24.590
You're late.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:29.700
I feel dreadful, moaned Bertie, all upset inside.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.660
and driver says he can't make me better.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.260
Thank goodness you're late, too.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.600
Can you take my passengers, please?

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.790
They'll never get home otherwise.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.490
Of course, agreed Thomas.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:45.040
He now felt sorry for Bertie,

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:47.530
promised to get help at the next station.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:49.650
Thomas set off again.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.320
Already, he felt much more cheerful,

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.280
and Bertie's passengers,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.220
traveling in Annie and Clarabel,

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.140
all reached home safely.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.000
When Bertie was better, he came to thank Thomas.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.620
I am sorry I teased you about being late, he said.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.730
That's all right, said Thomas.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.370
I'm glad I could help.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.600
There are times when being late isn't such a bad thing after all.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:20.380
With a last cheerful greeting, the two friends went back to work.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:37.410
So you see, the bad news is that when one train is late, it can throw everybody off.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:43.460
But the good news is that Bertie kept his promise, and things did get back to normal again.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:53.540
I'm sure that's what will happen with the Indian Valley Railroad, once they fix up this scheduling problem.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:58.140
Excuse me, could everyone please come into Harry's workshop for a meeting?

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:06.800
And this becomes a local for Doodlehaven.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.280
This meeting is called to order.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.320
I wish you'd warn me when you're going to do that.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.620
Sorry, Harry. I'll try to remember.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.320
Is that a track grid?

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:21.150
Sort of.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.610
It's my own sketch of the Indian Valley Railroad

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:28.640
with some new ideas for how to reschedule the trains.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:29.960
This is what I...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.530
wanted to show you. Harry and I think we figured out a way to reschedule the main line so that

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:40.610
nobody has to be late. Plus, we think it'll bring more business to the station, so we want to go to

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:48.520
the main office and discuss it with Mr. J.B. King. Esquire. J.B. King? He's the superintendent

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:55.810
of the whole Indian Valley line. When are you going to see him? Well, we'd like to go as soon

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:59.350
as possible, but we can't leave you kids here alone.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.400
Did I hear a cry for help?

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.620
I wondered where he was today.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.620
Excuse me, while I slip away.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.680
Did I hear you correctly, Miss Jones?

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.730
You need someone to manage the station

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:19.790
and to keep a loving eye on these adorable tykes.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.970
Hey, Schemer, how come all of a sudden

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.150
you think we're so adorable?

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.840
Just for the day, Schemer,

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:29.940
Harry and I have to go to the main office, but I...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.220
I don't think this is the kind of thing that you...

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.740
A common misconception.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.520
You're thinking Schemer,

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:39.340
the foremost entrepreneurial go-getter of our time

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:41.320
in a babysitting-type capacity?

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:45.230
But, Miss Jones, there is another side to me.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.610
What side would that be, Schemer?

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:52.730
Well, Harry, the love side.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:57.960
The caring, giving, kissing, hugging side.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.700
Well, I don't know.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:07.600
10.35 Express, Stacey, the last train to the office till tonight.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.120
Well, Schemer, if I was to leave you in charge,

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.320
you'd have to remember to call the train dispatcher

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.040
within the next half hour and tell him that there's a broken signal on track two.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.580
You got that, Schemer? It's too important to forget.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.720
Ms. Jones, I would remember that so much, I can't even tell you.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.390
Well, okay.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:25.410
Oh, goody.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:29.970
Now, remember, Schemer, I'm giving you the opportunity to prove how reliable...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:42.500
you can be run the station and help the passengers i completely and solemnly promise oh and you

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:49.550
must absolutely not leave the station or leave the children alone promise promise schemer a herd of

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:56.450
wild wombats could not drag me from their side well all right bye kids yes

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:01.950
Ms. Jones.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:02.430
Yes.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:03.620
Thank you.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:04.420
Oh, okay.

