00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.620
First he's changed things

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:40.740
around, and now he's left you

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:43.640
both alone. Can't you stop him?

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.120
My magic can do many things,

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:48.280
Matt, but it only works if you

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.280
believe in it. And Schema

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.290
only believes in himself. You said

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:55.330
it. You know, all this trouble with

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.500
Schema reminds me of when Diesel

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.480
first met the engines on the island of

00:14:59.480 --> 00:14:59.840
Sodor.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.550
He immediately got off on the wrong foot.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.260
Or the wrong wheel.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:06.380
Anyway, let me explain.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:12.950
Duck is very proud of being Great Western.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:15.300
He talks endlessly about it.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:19.660
But he works hard, too, and makes everything go like clockwork.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.880
It was a splendid day.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.640
The cars and coaches behaved well.

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.860
The passengers even stopped grumbling.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.080
But the engines didn't like having to bustle about.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:48.130
There are two ways of doing things, Duck told them.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.050
The Great Western way or the wrong way.

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:54.160
I'm Great Western and don't we know it.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:58.360
The engines were glad when a visitor came.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.660
He purred smoothly towards them.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:12.090
Sir Topham has introduced him.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:13.380
Here is Diesel.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.760
I have agreed to give him a trial.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:17.330
He needs to learn.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:18.920
Please teach him, duck.

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:23.150
Good morning, purred Diesel in an oily voice.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.620
Pleased to meet you, duck.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.660
Is that James and Henry and Gordon?

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.340
I'm delighted to meet such famous engine.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:42.200
The silly engines were flattered.

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:46.030
He has very good manners, they murmured.

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.440
We are pleased to have him in our yard.

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:52.240
Duck had his doubts.

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:54.090
Come on, he said.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:55.710
Diesel purred after him.

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:04.690
You're worthy, Sir Topham Hatt, to you, or to Duck.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:07.890
Diesel looked hurt.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:12.080
You're worthy, Sir Topham Hatt, thinks I need to learn.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.820
He is mistaken.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.530
We diesels don't need to learn.

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:18.330
We know everything.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.390
We come to a yard and improve it.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:23.510
We are revolutionary.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:29.650
Oh, said Duck, if you're reverthingamy, perhaps you would collect my cars.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.700
while I fetch Gordon's coaches.

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:35.060
Diesel, delighted to show off, purred away.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.950
When Duck returned, Diesel was trying to take

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.270
some cars from a siding.

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:42.850
They were old and empty.

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:45.680
They have not been touched for a long time.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.120
Diesel found them hard to move.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.700
Pull, push, backwards, forwards, oink.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.890
The cars groaned.

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:58.920
We can't.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:09.600
we won't. Duck watched with interest. Diesel lost patience. He roared, gave a great heave.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:18.110
The cars jerked forward. They screamed, we can't, we won't. Some of their brakes snapped

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:28.750
and the gear jammed in the sleepers. Chuckled Duck. Diesel recovered and tried to push the

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.970
cars back but they

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:35.330
wouldn't move duck run quietly round to collect the other cars thank you for

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:40.850
arranging these diesel I must go now don't you want this lot no thank you

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:46.770
diesel gulped and I've taken all this trouble why didn't you tell me you

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:51.910
never asked me besides said duck you were having such fun being rev whatever

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:53.510
it was you said goodbye

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.360
Diesel had to help the workmen clear the mess.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.340
